  m_Text: "How to robot is a VR training experience created as a student project
    to explore how virtual reality can help people interact more safely and confidently
    with humanoid robots. \n\nIn our simulation, you step into a realistic everyday
    environment and learn the fundamentals of safe operation. \nFrom basic start-up
    procedures and safe distances to emergency responses and shutdown routines.\n\nOur
    goal is not to replace professional instruction, but to offer an accessible introduction
    that reduces uncertainty and supports safer behavior before users encounter real
    robotic systems.\n\nThe training focuses on practical, easy-to-understand scenarios
    and combines short theory segments with hands-on tasks, so that learning remains
    clear, structured, and engaging.\n\n\nIMPORTANT: This project provides a simplified
    training simulation. Real robots and real environments can behave unpredictably,
    and no VR experience can fully cover every possible hazard, malfunction, or human
    error. \nWhile we aim to reflect common safety principles and realistic situations,
    we cannot guarantee that all risks are detected or prevented. \nAlways follow
    official manuals, safety guidelines, and professional instructions when working
    with actual robots.\n\nThank you for trying our prototype. We hope it sparks
    curiosity, supports safer interactions, and shows how VR training could evolve
    in the future."
